---
description: Ensure only available Spectrum icons are used in the project
globs: ["**/*.tsx", "**/*.ts", "**/*.jsx", "**/*.js"]
alwaysApply: false
---

# Spectrum Icons Usage Rule

This rule ensures that only available Spectrum icons are used throughout the project, preventing broken icon imports and maintaining consistency.

<rule>
name: spectrum_icons_only
description: Enforce usage of only available Spectrum icons from approved sources
filters:
  # Match React/TypeScript files that might contain icon imports
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.(tsx?|jsx?)$"
  # Match icon import statements
  - type: content
    pattern: "import.*from.*['\"].*icons?.*['\"]"

actions:

- type: suggest
  message: |

  ## Available Icon Sources

  ### 1. React Spectrum S2 Icons

  ```typescript
  // ✅ Correct usage
  import Edit from "@react-spectrum/s2/icons/Edit";
  import Contrast from "@react-spectrum/s2/icons/Contrast";
  import FileText from "@react-spectrum/s2/icons/FileText";
  import Folder from "@react-spectrum/s2/icons/Folder";
  ```

  ### 2. SWC React Workflow Icons

  ```typescript
  // ✅ Correct usage
  import { IconHome } from "@swc-react/icons-workflow/Home";
  import { IconAsset } from "@swc-react/icons-workflow/Asset";
  import { IconApps } from "@swc-react/icons-workflow/Apps";
  import { IconMore } from "@swc-react/icons-workflow/More";
  import { IconSend } from "@swc-react/icons-workflow/Send";
  import { IconLayers } from "@swc-react/icons-workflow/Layers";
  import { IconAttach } from "@swc-react/icons-workflow/Attach";
  import { IconMicrophone } from "@swc-react/icons-workflow/Microphone";
  ```

  ### 3. Custom SVG Icons (when Spectrum icons don't exist)

  ```typescript
  // ✅ Correct usage - custom icons as React components
  import { IconAiChat } from "../../assets/svgs/iconAiChat.tsx";
  import { IconCreate } from "../../assets/svgs/iconCreate.tsx";
  import { IconCampaign } from "../../assets/svgs/iconCampaign.tsx";
  ```

  ## Icon Usage Guidelines
  **Reuse semantic category icons first.** For project concepts, use `CategoryIcon` from `src/components/CategoryIcon.ts` (or `getCategoryIcon` when a component type is required). `src/data/category-icons.json` is the single mapping source: `"modes"` currently maps to `Filters`, and `"tokens"` to `Channel`. Do not hardcode a similar glyph or duplicate the mapping in a component.

  1. **Prefer Spectrum S2 icons first** - Check if the icon exists in `@react-spectrum/s2/icons`. S2 icons work natively in S2 components with no wrapper needed.
  2. **Use custom SVG icons only when necessary** - When Spectrum doesn't have the needed icon
  3. **Create proper React components** - Custom icons should be React components, not direct SVG imports
  4. **Follow naming conventions** - Use PascalCase for icon component names
  5. **Organize custom icons** - Place all custom SVG icons in `assets/svgs/` directory

  ## Authored mode-set icons

  Use `modeSetGroupIconId` from `src/features/modes/controlPresentation.ts`
  for menu entries representing a whole mode set. It prefers the set's own
  icon, then the default mode's icon only when the existing
  `modeSetUsesOptionIcons` rule permits unique option icons. Render the ID
  with `MODE_ICONS` from `src/features/modes/icons.ts`; use
  `<CategoryIcon category="modes" />` when it returns `"none"`.
  This keeps authored identity separate from temporary preview selection.
  Do not repeat this precedence or select the first/current mode in menus.

  In the conditional builder's Add condition menu, Mode set uses `"modes"`;
  Token category uses `"tokens"`. Token-category submenu entries are text-only
  because repeating the same icon adds no distinction. Keep icon-plus-label content
  in the S2 icon slot plus `Text`, not raw text beside an icon.

  ## Label text next to icons

  When an S2 control shows an icon and visible label text together (for example `Button` with an icon slot and a caption), wrap the label in **`Text`** from `@react-spectrum/s2`. Do not leave raw text nodes as siblings of the icon. This keeps typography and layout aligned with Spectrum 2.

  ```typescript
  import { ActionButton, Button, Text } from "@react-spectrum/s2";
  ```

  ```tsx
  // ✅ Correct: label wrapped in Text
  <Button variant="secondary" size="M">
    <IconSlotWrapper>
      <IconHome />
    </IconSlotWrapper>
    <Text>Home</Text>
  </Button>

  // ❌ Wrong: raw text next to the icon
  <Button variant="secondary" size="M">
    <IconSlotWrapper>
      <IconHome />
    </IconSlotWrapper>
    Home
  </Button>
  ```

  Icon-only controls (no visible label) do not need `Text`. Controls that are text-only with no icon do not need `Text` for the label unless a pattern elsewhere in the product requires it.

  ## CRITICAL: Wrapping non-S2 icons in S2 components

  Any icon that does NOT come from `@react-spectrum/s2/icons` must be wrapped
  with `IconSlotWrapper` when placed inside an S2 component (ActionButton,
  ToggleButton, Button, etc.). This includes SWC workflow icons and custom SVG
  icons. Without the wrapper, the button will appear stretched because S2
  components use `:has([slot="icon"])` CSS selectors that non-S2 icons do not
  satisfy.

  ```typescript
  import { IconSlotWrapper } from "../components/IconSlotWrapper";
  ```

  ```tsx
  // ✅ Correct: S2 icon — no wrapper needed
  <ActionButton isQuiet aria-label="Toggle color scheme">
    <Contrast />
  </ActionButton>

  // ✅ Correct: Non-S2 icon wrapped with IconSlotWrapper
  <ActionButton isQuiet aria-label="Home">
    <IconSlotWrapper><IconHome /></IconSlotWrapper>
  </ActionButton>

  // ❌ Wrong: Non-S2 icon without wrapper — button will be stretched
  <ActionButton isQuiet aria-label="Home">
    <IconHome />
  </ActionButton>
  ```

  See `docs/non-s2-icons-in-s2-components.md` for the full technical explanation.

examples:

- input: |
  // ❌ Bad: Unknown icon library
  import { FaHome } from "react-icons/fa";

  // ❌ Bad: Direct SVG import  
   import homeIcon from "./home.svg";

  // ❌ Bad: Non-existent Spectrum icon
  import CustomIcon from "@react-spectrum/s2/icons/CustomIcon";

  // ❌ Bad: Non-S2 icon without IconSlotWrapper in S2 component
  <ActionButton isQuiet aria-label="Home">
  <IconHome />
  </ActionButton>
  output: |
  // ✅ Good: Use available Spectrum icons
  import { IconHome } from "@swc-react/icons-workflow/Home";
  import { IconSlotWrapper } from "../components/IconSlotWrapper";

  // ✅ Good: Custom icon as React component
  import { IconCustom } from "../../assets/svgs/iconCustom.tsx";

  // ✅ Good: Non-S2 icon wrapped for S2 component
  <ActionButton isQuiet aria-label="Home">
  <IconSlotWrapper><IconHome /></IconSlotWrapper>
  </ActionButton>

  // ✅ Good: icon + label — use Text for the label
  import { Button, Text } from "@react-spectrum/s2";
  <Button variant="secondary">
  <IconSlotWrapper><IconHome /></IconSlotWrapper>
  <Text>Home</Text>
  </Button>

metadata:
priority: high
version: 2.1
category: icons
enforcement: strict
</rule>
